update public.instructors set short_bio = 'Haitian-American artist working in photography, video, and audio.', biography = $bio$Gérardine Aldamar is a first-generation Haitian-American artist based in Philadelphia. She holds a BFA in Photography and Digital Arts from Moore College of Art & Design. She primarily works in the photographic medium along with video and audio works. Her current project, Fanmi, uses appropriated family photos where she adds digital alterations that are informed by old family stories, adding a new context to the images. The work is a meditation on the everchanging familial roles after a loved one has passed and how one chooses to honor and keep them with us going forward. Her work has been featured as part of the Little Berlin Collective at The Front in New Orleans, the Cado Marketplace at the Hatfield House in Philadelphia, Tet Ansanm, a duo exhibition at Allen’s Lane Art Center, and the Emerge Exhibition at Bond Millen Gallery in Richmond, VA.$bio$ where source_instructor_id = '10893';
update public.instructors set short_bio = 'Philadelphia artist whose work draws on family, heritage, and altered states.', biography = $bio$Inga Kimberly Brown was born and raised in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. She received an MFA (2014–2016) from the University of North Carolina at Greensboro and a BFA (2010–2014) from The Pennsylvania Academy of Fine Arts. “I was born an artist and I believe art making is my first language of communication. I want to engage in a community that communicates in that first language no matter the medium.” Inga’s inspiration derives from her family and racial mixed heritage as well as her spiritual and sensitive sense of altered states and various astro planes that exist around us.$bio$ where source_instructor_id = '8389';
update public.instructors set short_bio = 'Philadelphia painter and printmaker who teaches students of all ages.', biography = $bio$Romy Burkus is a painter/printmaker from Philadelphia, Pennsylvania who enjoys teaching all ages, from kindergarten through college. Her diverse background in drawing, painting, graphic design, printmaking, bookarts, and ceramics allows her flexibility when creating a series of work. Romy has exhibited her art consistently for the past 30 years, mostly in the Philadelphia area. She has a BFA from Moore College of Art and Design, an MAT in Teaching from the University of the Arts, and has attended many classes at the Pennsylvania Academy of Fine Arts, Peters Valley Art Center, The Clay Studio, and Bennington College. Romy enjoys seeing her students expand their art skills and encouraging the cross-pollinating of various areas of the visual arts. Currently she teaches middle school students at Germantown Academy in Fort Washington, PA.$bio$ where source_instructor_id = '9752';
update public.instructors set short_bio = 'Philadelphia performer, musician, writer, and theater educator.', biography = $bio$Sarah Clemency is a performer, musician, writer, comedian local to Philadelphia. She has her B.A. in Theater and Music. Sarah has been teaching all ages theater and music for over 15 years. She has taught and performed improv with Crossroads Comedy, SideQuest Theater, and Sawubona Creativity Project. Bringing the arts to all people is her passion.$bio$ where source_instructor_id = '12197';
update public.instructors set short_bio = 'Artist working across painting, printmaking, and digital imaging.', biography = $bio$Albert Fung (he, him), born 1970 in San Francisco, California, makes work that is meaningful when it rings like a bell, shocks like the new, and bothers like memory. His work is kinesthetic and synaesthetic: a sensation of color leaves a taste in one’s mouth; pictorial rhythms land like body blows. He has been producing artwork in oil, acrylic, watercolor, pastel, intaglio, lithography, and digital imaging for over thirty years. He attended Rochester Institute of Technology (BFA–Printmaking) and Massachusetts College of Art (MFA–Painting and Printmaking). He has shown throughout Philadelphia and New York, and lives and works in Philadelphia.$bio$ where source_instructor_id = '8295';
update public.instructors set short_bio = 'Theater artist, playwright, director, author, and educator.', biography = $bio$Barbara L. Gregson is a theater artist, playwright, director, and author with 45 years of experience creating and performing original theater. She has written and performed her own one-woman shows with live music, on stages ranging from intimate venues to large-scale productions, and on street corners with her street theater troupe in cities across Europe and the United States. Barbara studied ancient theater techniques in Europe and the US, including mask making, mask performance, mime, movement, acting, and storytelling. She weaves these techniques into her plays, performances, and productions, which are accompanied by live original music. As a teacher and director, Barbara brings these same ancient techniques to people of all ages and abilities. She guides participants to create, make, and perform their own original theater wherever they are, including schools, museums, senior centers, hospitals, and correctional facilities.$bio$, website_url = 'https://www.gregson.theater/index.html' where source_instructor_id = '12324';
update public.instructors set short_bio = 'Bookarts and printmaking educator with deep museum-learning experience.', biography = $bio$Rebecca has a BA in Art History and an MFA in Bookarts/Printmaking. After working in the commercial printing industry and museum publishing, she became an art teacher. She recently retired after over two decades as a Museum Educator at the Philadelphia Museum of Art where she had the opportunity to write many educational materials for children. She also illustrated a coloring book that has been reprinted several times and given to thousands of preschool students before their visit to the museum.$bio$ where source_instructor_id = '8400';
update public.instructors set short_bio = 'Ceramicist and teaching artist specializing in handbuilt work.', biography = $bio$Linda Johnson is a professional ceramicist and teaching artist based in Huntingdon Valley, PA. Linda’s work explores the illustrative elements of nature through handbuilt ceramic vessels and wall art. Linda incorporates original imagery of birds and floral motifs to adorn her pieces, often evoking a whimsical charm that draws in viewers. Linda earned her BFA in Sculpture with minors in art history and fibers from Tyler School of Art and studied sculpture and art history at the Burren College of Art in Co. Clare, Ireland. She joined the indie craft movement in the early 2000s and has stocked stores across the United States for the past 20 years under the brands Little Flower Designs and Linda Johnson Studio. Linda brings over 10 years of teaching experience, cultivating an inclusive studio community and enthusiasm for sharing her skills with students.$bio$ where source_instructor_id = '12198';
update public.instructors set short_bio = 'Philadelphia artist and educator who creates room for creative play.', biography = $bio$Hannah Judd is a passionate educator and artist based in Philadelphia who loves opening space for creative play. With a background in art spanning performance, ceramics, textile design, and illustration, she is most focused on personal expression and joy through any medium. Her teaching philosophy centers on the process of discovery, whether students are weaving their first wall hanging, building clay creatures, or diving into spontaneous theater games. When she’s not teaching, Hannah is active in improv comedy, poetry, and musical improv, as well as being a walker about town.$bio$ where source_instructor_id = '12196';
update public.instructors set short_bio = 'Dominican-Puerto Rican artist and educator specializing in drawing, painting, and assemblage.', biography = $bio$Emilio Maldonado is a Dominican-Puerto Rican artist and educator based in Philadelphia, whose work spans studio practice, education, and community engagement. His art has been showcased in group and solo exhibitions across the United States and internationally, including venues in Philadelphia, the Dominican Republic, Germany, and France. He has been honored with fellowships including the Mural Arts Philadelphia Black Artists Fellowship and the CFEVA Fellowship. He is also a Fitler Club Resident Artist and was named one of the 20 emerging Black artists to watch by the Philadelphia Inquirer in 2021. As an educator, he specializes in Drawing, Painting, 2D Design, and Assemblage Sculpture, fostering creativity and critical thinking among students.$bio$ where source_instructor_id = '10279';
update public.instructors set short_bio = 'Multimedia sculptor working in wood, fiber arts, and ceramics.', biography = $bio$Nicholas Malik is a multimedia sculptor working in wood, fiber arts, and ceramics. They most recently finished the Core Fellowship at the Penland School of Craft in North Carolina, where they learned skills from some of the best makers in their fields. Nicholas is very excited to share this knowledge with the Allens Lane community and hopes you’ll join in on building skills together.$bio$ where source_instructor_id = '10205';
update public.instructors set short_bio = 'Ceramic artist and educator focused on functional work.', biography = $bio$Samantha Moran (she/her) has a Bachelor’s degree from Tyler School of Art at Temple University and a Master’s in Art Education from University of the Arts. She has been working with clay for over a decade and gravitates toward creating functional ceramics. Samantha also works with The Clay Studio in Philadelphia for private events and teen clay camps.$bio$ where source_instructor_id = '8402';
update public.instructors set short_bio = 'Philadelphia ceramic artist, educator, consultant, and wholesaler.', biography = $bio$Mackenzie Pikaart is a ceramic artist based in Philadelphia. Her work is rooted in memory, emotion, and the quiet rhythms of daily life. She creates functional pieces that reflect moments of introspection, using form, color, and texture to explore the space between solitude and connection. Inspired by architecture, poetry, music, and rainy days, her ceramics invite reflection and care. Designed for daily use, each piece becomes part of personal rituals and shared experiences. Mackenzie holds a BFA in Crafts/Ceramics from The University of the Arts in Philadelphia, where she lives and works. In addition to her studio practice, she is a ceramics educator, consultant, and wholesaler.$bio$ where source_instructor_id = '11569';
update public.instructors set short_bio = 'Stained-glass artist, educator, and founder of Greg Stefan Studios.', biography = $bio$Greg Stefan is a stained glass artist, educator, and founder of Greg Stefan Studios in the Frankford neighborhood of Philadelphia. After completing an intensive eight-year apprenticeship in traditional stained glass techniques, Greg worked as a journeyman and project foreman for respected studios including Willet Hauser Architectural Glass and Femenella & Associates, before founding Greg Stefan Studios in 2004. With more than two decades of professional experience, Greg is committed to preserving the traditions of stained glass craftsmanship while inspiring new generations of artists. Through workshops, classes, and apprenticeships, he has taught hundreds of students, from beginners exploring the medium for the first time to advanced practitioners studying restoration techniques.$bio$ where source_instructor_id = '12091';
update public.instructors set short_bio = 'Ceramic artist and community-focused arts educator.', biography = $bio$Chloe Theodosiou is a ceramic artist whose practice focuses on where material experiments meet emotional articulation. Originally from New York, Theodosiou graduated with her BFA from Alfred University and worked as a teaching, assisting, and exhibiting artist in NYC for four years before moving to Phoenixville, PA. She has been living in Pennsylvania since 2020, working with local art spaces and nonprofits to provide affordable, high-quality art education. She is motivated by community and humanity in the arts with an intense passion for all things clay.$bio$, image_url = 'https://alnimages.artcentercanvas.com/library/artist//9341_9501.jpg' where source_instructor_id = '9341';
update public.instructors set short_bio = 'Mixed-media artist and experienced art and museum educator.', biography = $bio$Bex is a mixed media artist based in Southwest Philly. They have over 15 years of experience as an art and museum educator, and have facilitated close-looking and making workshops with students of all ages in museums, galleries, community centers, and classrooms across Greater Philadelphia. They are thrilled to be joining the Allen’s Lane Arts Center teaching artist cohort and can’t wait to see what creations take shape in After School Studio.$bio$ where source_instructor_id = '12195';
update public.instructors set short_bio = 'Ceramic artist and longtime teacher of functional pottery.', biography = $bio$Nathan Willever was raised in Portsmouth, New Hampshire. He holds a Bachelor of Fine Arts in Ceramics from Maine College of Art in Portland, Maine. He has taught numerous classes and workshops on functional pottery at institutions including The Clay Studio in Philadelphia, PA, Ox-Bow School of Art in Saugatuck, Michigan, and Haystack Mountain School of Crafts in Deer Isle, ME. Nathan is currently a long-term Resident and Zeldin Fellow at The Clay Studio.$bio$ where source_instructor_id = '8405';
update public.instructors set short_bio = 'Associate Artist at The Clay Studio and traditional pottery educator.', biography = $bio$Robin Williams Turnage is currently an Associate Artist at The Clay Studio as well as a teacher of Traditional Nigerian and Ghanaian Pottery with Jihan Thomas at Fleisher. Robin’s art has always reflected an African aesthetic. Currently, she is working in the production of porcelain tableware with an African influence. Robin has exhibited her work more actively in recent years in places like the gallery at The Clay Studio, Fleisher, The Colored Girls Museum, and with The Drummond Art Legacy.$bio$ where source_instructor_id = '8406';
